.TH FERMISSOSESSION 3 "2026-09-02" "requests-fermi-sso 0.2.0" "Python Library"
.SH NAME
FermiSSOSession \- requests.Session subclass that logs into Fermilab SSO
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
.B from requests_fermi_sso import FermiSSOSession
.sp
.BI "s = FermiSSOSession(userpass=f\(dq{" user } : { pass }\(dq)
.BI "r = s.get(\(dq" URL \(dq)
.sp
.BI "s = FermiSSOSession(cookie_file=\(dq" PATH \(dq)
.BI "n = s.load_cookies(" PATH ", fmt=None, missing_ok=False)"
.BI "n = s.save_cookies(" PATH ", fmt=None)"
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B FermiSSOSession
subclasses
.B requests.Session
and overrides
.BR send() .
Every response is inspected before it is handed back; if it looks like a
stage of the Fermilab PingFederate single sign\-on sequence, the session
answers it and continues, so the caller receives the protected page rather
than the login machinery.
.PP
Callers use it exactly like a normal
.BR requests.Session .
There is no explicit login call, and no state to manage beyond keeping the
session object alive.
.SS Flow
The overridden
.B send()
recognizes and answers four pages, in order:
.TP
.B django\-allauth confirmation page
Served by Django applications that use allauth for Fermilab SSO at
.I /accounts/<provider>/login/
or
.IR /accounts/oidc/<id>/login/ :
a
.B method="post"
form whose only field is
.B csrfmiddlewaretoken
(optionally also
.BR next ),
posting back to the page's own URL. The session posts it, with a
same\-origin
.B Referer
for Django's CSRF check, and the application then redirects to the identity
provider. Forms posting anywhere else, notably the site's own
.I /accounts/logout/
"Sign out" button, are never submitted.
.TP
.B Choose\-authentication page
A form with
.B method="GET"
and an action under
.I /idp/
(SAML) or
.I /as/
(OIDC / OAuth2).
The session re\-requests it with
.B pfidpadapterid=ad..FormBased
and
.BR rememberChoice=true ,
selecting password authentication.
.TP
.B Login page
A form with
.B method="POST"
and an action under
.I /idp/
or
.IR /as/ .
The session posts
.BR pf.username ,
.BR pf.pass ,
.BR pf.ok ,
.BR pf.cancel ,
and
.BR pf.adapterId .
This step is skipped when the session was constructed without
.BR userpass .
.TP
.B SAML postback form
An auto\-submitting form carrying
.B RelayState
and
.BR SAMLResponse .
The session posts it to the service provider, which sets the application
session cookie.
.PP
OIDC flows have no postback form: the identity provider answers the login
POST with a redirect to the application's callback, which
.B requests
follows on its own, so the sequence ends one step earlier.
.PP
A
.B logging_in_already
flag suppresses this handling for the nested requests the session issues
itself, preventing unbounded recursion. It is cleared before
.B send()
returns.
.SS Cookie reuse
Every cookie the identity provider and service provider set during a login
lives in the session jar, so within one process only the first request pays
for the login. With
.B cookie_file
that jar is loaded before the first request and written back after each
completed login sequence, so the next process, or any other script pointed
at the same file, is already logged in and needs no password at all.
.PP
The file may equally be a browser's exported
.IR cookies.txt .
That is the only route for an account enrolled in multi\-factor
authentication: log in once in a browser, export the cookies for the
service provider, and hand them to the session. Note that the session
cookies are bearer credentials; the file is written mode 0600 and should be
treated like a password.
.SH CONSTRUCTOR
.TP
.BI FermiSSOSession( "\fR...\fP" ", userpass=" STRING ", cookie_file=" PATH ", cookie_format=" FMT ", cookie_save=" BOOL )
The keywords below are consumed; all other arguments are passed to
.BR requests.Session .
.RS
.TP
.B userpass
Split on
.RB \(dq : \(dq
into a username and password for the identity provider's password adapter.
.TP
.B cookie_file
Path of a cookie jar, with
.B ~
expanded. It is loaded immediately; a file that does not exist yet is
ignored so a first run can create it. The number of cookies loaded is left in
.BR cookies_loaded .
.TP
.B cookie_format
One of
.BR netscape ", " lwp ", or " json .
Defaults to
.BR None ,
meaning detect from the file extension
.RI ( .json ", " .lwp )
and then the first line; unrecognized files are read as Netscape
.IR cookies.txt ,
and new files are written in that format.
.TP
.B cookie_save
When true the jar is rewritten to
.B cookie_file
after any request that completed a login sequence or otherwise changed the
jar, for example a second site behind the same identity provider signing
the session in through a bare redirect chain. Defaults to true whenever
.B cookie_file
is given. A request that leaves the jar unchanged never touches the file, so
a browser export is not rewritten unless the site issued new cookies.
.RE
.PP
Without
.BR userpass ,
the session still selects an authentication method and submits postback
forms, but never fills in the login form. Combined with
.B cookie_file
this is the cookies\-only mode; alone, it is useful for inspecting the flow
without credentials.
.SH ATTRIBUTES
.TP
.B login_form_data
The dict posted to the login form, or
.B None
when no
.B userpass
was given.
.TP
.B choose_page_re
.TQ
.B login_page_re
.TQ
.B postback_form_re
.TQ
.B base_re
Compiled patterns used to recognize each page. Exposed so callers can test
a response themselves, which is how
.BR fermi_sso_probe (1)
distinguishes a failed login from a successful one.
.TP
.B adapterid
The identity provider adapter to select. Defaults to
.BR ad..FormBased .
.TP
.B logging_in_already
Recursion guard; true only while a login sequence is in progress.
.TP
.B allauth_url_re
Pattern the response URL path must match before a page is considered an
allauth confirmation page. Defaults to
.BR ^/accounts/.+/login/?$ .
.TP
.B allauth_count
Number of allauth confirmation forms this session has submitted.
.TP
.B cookie_file
.TQ
.B cookie_format
.TQ
.B cookie_save
The constructor arguments of the same names, after
.B ~
expansion.
.TP
.B cookies_loaded
Number of cookies read from
.B cookie_file
by the constructor.
.TP
.B login_count
Number of login sequences this session has completed. Zero after a request
that the loaded cookies satisfied outright, which is how
.BR fermi_sso_probe (1)
reports whether cookie reuse worked.
.SH METHODS
Beyond the inherited
.B requests.Session
interface:
.TP
.BI send( request ", " **kwargs )
Overridden. Performs the request, then advances the login flow if needed.
.TP
.BI extract_login_url( response )
Absolute URL of the login form, honoring any
.B <base>
tag.
.TP
.BI extract_chose_url( response )
Absolute URL that selects password authentication, query string included.
.TP
.BI extract_post_back_data( response )
Returns
.RI ( url ", " formdata )
for the SAML postback form.
.TP
.BI is_allauth_sso_page( response )
True when the response is an allauth confirmation page as defined under
Flow.
.TP
.BI extract_allauth_form( response )
Returns
.RI ( url ", " formdata )
for the confirmation form: the absolute URL it posts to and its hidden
fields.
.TP
.BI load_cookies( path ", fmt=None, missing_ok=False)"
Merge the cookies in
.I path
into the session jar, skipping expired ones, and return the number loaded.
.I fmt
is detected as for the constructor when
.BR None .
A missing file raises
.B FileNotFoundError
unless
.B missing_ok
is set, in which case 0 is returned.
.TP
.BI save_cookies( path ", fmt=None)"
Write the unexpired cookies in the jar to
.IR path ,
creating it mode 0600 via a temporary file and rename, and return the number
written. Session cookies, which have no expiry, are written with expiry 0
rather than dropped as
.B http.cookiejar
would. With
.I fmt
.B None
the format follows the extension, defaulting to Netscape.
.SH COOKIE FILE FORMATS
.TP
.B netscape
The tab\-separated
.I cookies.txt
written by
.BR curl (1)
.BR \-c ,
.BR wget (1),
and the common browser export extensions. Seven fields per line: domain,
include\-subdomains flag, path, secure flag, expiry (0 for a session cookie),
name, value. HttpOnly cookies carry a
.B #HttpOnly_
prefix on the domain; this module reads and writes that prefix itself
because
.B http.cookiejar.MozillaCookieJar
before Python 3.10 discards such lines as comments, which would drop exactly
the SSO cookies that matter.
.TP
.B lwp
The Set\-Cookie3 format of
.BR http.cookiejar.LWPCookieJar .
.TP
.B json
A list of objects with keys
.BR name ", " value ", " domain ", " path ", " secure ", " httponly ", " host_only ", " expires
(seconds since the epoch, or null for a session cookie). On input the
camel\-case keys of the Cookie\-Editor and EditThisCookie browser extensions
.RB ( expirationDate ", " httpOnly ", " hostOnly ", " session )
are accepted too, as is a top\-level object with a
.B cookies
list.
.SH FILES
The library imposes no default path.
.BR fermi_sso_probe (1)
uses whatever
.B \-\-cookie\-file
or
.B FERMI_SSO_COOKIE_FILE
names.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.B send()
returns a
.B requests.Response
for the final page of the sequence.
.SH ERRORS
A failed login is
.B not
signalled by an exception or a non\-2xx status. The identity provider
re\-serves its login page with status 200, so the response looks ordinary.
Callers must inspect the body; see
.BR fermi_sso_probe (1),
which implements that check.
.PP
A
.B userpass
value containing more than one colon raises
.B ValueError
from the constructor, because the password cannot be told from the
delimiter.
.SH EXAMPLES
Fetch a protected page:
.PP
.RS
.EX
from requests_fermi_sso import FermiSSOSession

s = FermiSSOSession(userpass="myaccount:mypassword")
r = s.get("https://mu2e\-docdb.fnal.gov/cgi\-bin/sso/DocumentDatabase")
if s.login_page_re.search(r.text):
    raise SystemExit("login failed")
print(r.text)
.EE
.RE
.PP
Cookies persist on the session, so later requests to the same service
provider skip the login round trip entirely. The identity provider's own
session cookie persists too, so a jar filled by logging in to one site
usually signs the session in to a second site behind the same IdP with no
login sequence at all; the second site's cookies are then added to the jar.
.PP
Log in once, then reuse the jar from a later process with no password:
.PP
.RS
.EX
# first run, or whenever the jar has gone stale
s = FermiSSOSession(userpass="myaccount:mypassword",
                    cookie_file="~/.fermi_sso.cookies")
s.get("https://mu2e\-docdb.fnal.gov/cgi\-bin/sso/DocumentDatabase")

# later runs
s = FermiSSOSession(cookie_file="~/.fermi_sso.cookies")
r = s.get("https://mu2e\-docdb.fnal.gov/cgi\-bin/DocDB/ShowDocument?docid=1234")
if s.login_page_re.search(r.text):
    raise SystemExit("cookies expired; run the password login again")
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use a browser session for an MFA\-enrolled account. In the browser, log in
to the service provider, export its cookies with a cookies.txt extension,
then:
.PP
.RS
.EX
s = FermiSSOSession(cookie_file="/path/to/cookies.txt", cookie_save=False)
r = s.get("https://mu2e\-docdb.fnal.gov/cgi\-bin/sso/DocumentDatabase")
.EE
.RE
.PP
Sign in to a Django application that uses allauth in front of Fermilab SSO.
The application's own sign\-in page is a menu; fetch the "Log in with
Fermilab SSO" link's URL and the session handles the confirmation form, the
identity provider, and the callback:
.PP
.RS
.EX
start = "https://mu2e\-talks.fnal.gov/accounts/oidc/keycloak/login/?next=%2F"
r = s.get(start)          # lands on the dashboard
.EE
.RE
.SH LIMITATIONS
Only the
.B ad..FormBased
password adapter is driven; accounts requiring multi\-factor authentication
cannot complete the login flow themselves and must supply cookies from a
browser session instead. Where the service provider's connection demands a
second factor regardless, as Workday's does (RSA SecurID after the
password), the flow stops at the passcode form. JavaScript redirect pages
and auto\-submitting SAML
.B AuthnRequest
forms, both seen in front of third\-party services, are not followed. The
identity provider keeps separate sessions for its OIDC and SAML connections,
so a jar filled at an OIDC site still needs one password login at the first
SAML site. Cookie reuse lasts only as long as the service
provider's session; the library does not know the lifetime in advance and
detects expiry only by landing on the login page again. Page recognition is
regular\-expression based and
will break if the identity provider changes its markup. The session holds
per\-login state and must not be shared across threads.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fermi_sso_probe (1)
.PP
